 \section{Limitations and Future Work}
 \label{sec:limitations}
 
-This evaluation is scoped to the GUMBO FSE Rule book and the 42-unit Isolette Monitor/Regulate target exercised through HAMR/INSPECTA. It shows encouraging intra-system reuse from a small solved file/subsystem example to remaining target files, but does not establish broad cross-system generality or quantitatively validate broader HAMR rule books. The one-time extraction/refinement effort is reported in the adjusted run and should be amortized only after additional reuse is measured. Future work will evaluate broader rule books for SysML structure, Slang compatibility, seL4/Microkit mappings, Rust/Verus repair, and additional systems, including seL4-based firewall architectures~\cite{Hatcliff:seL4Summit2025} and repair heuristics inspired by \textsc{VeriStruct}~\cite{sun2025veristruct}. We will also study cloud-scale verification, multimodal specification, and compositional reasoning advances in GUMBO/AGREE~\cite{compositional-analysis-agree,agreedog_tahat2025}.
+This evaluation is scoped to the GUMBO FSE Rule book and to the Isolette Monitor/Regulate target exercised through the HAMR/INSPECTA workflow. The results provide encouraging evidence of intra-system reuse: rules learned from a small solved file/subsystem example were reused to support verification of the remaining target files. However, the current study does not establish broad cross-system generality, and additional HAMR rule books have not yet been quantitatively validated across independent systems. The one-time learning effort is therefore reported in the adjusted run; broader amortization should be claimed only after additional reuse has been measured. Future work will evaluate rule books for SysML synthesis, Slang compatibility, seL4/Microkit mappings, Rust/Verus repair, and additional systems, including seL4-based firewall architectures~\cite{Hatcliff:seL4Summit2025} and repair heuristics inspired by \textsc{VeriStruct}~\cite{sun2025veristruct}. We will also study cloud-scale verification, multimodal specification, and advances in compositional reasoning for GUMBO/AGREE~\cite{compositional-analysis-agree,agreedog_tahat2025}.
